       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day, and it risks serious hepatotoxicity. Some centers use a lower ceiling of 3,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also above the usual 1,000 mg maximum per dose.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you really do want 3000 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting the intent. Otherwise, tell me which of the regimens above you want and I'll enter it."
