     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is in the range that causes acute liver failure, and I know of no indication that would justify it for a 70 kg adult. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the goal is stronger pain or fever control, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. If you're treating an acetaminophen overdose, that follows a different protocol, usually N-acetylcysteine dosed by level. If you think the dose is right and I'm missing something, please talk with pharmacy about it. I won't place it myself.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
